1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Every bloodline has a beginning.

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Dracula Untold is a horror, action, fantasy film directed by Gary Shore.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Vlad Tepes is a great hero, but when he learns the Sultan is preparing for battle and needs
to form an army of 1,000 boys, he vows to find a way to protect his family.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Vlad turns to dark forces in order to get the power to destroy his enemies and agrees to go
from hero to monster as he's turned into the mythological vampire, Dracula.

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Vlad Tepes / Dracula, played by Luke Evans.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Mirena / Mina Murray, played by Sarah Gadon.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Mehmed II, played by Dominic Cooper.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Ingeras, played by Art Parkinson.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Master Vampire, played by Charles Dance.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Dimitru, played by Diarmaid Murtagh.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
Dracula Untold is a 2014 American action horror film directed by Gary Shore in his
feature film debut, and written by Matt Sazama and Burk Sharpless.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Based on an original screenplay by Sazama and Sharpless, the plot creates an origin story for
the title character, rather than using the storyline of Bram Stoker's Dracula.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
In this adaptation, Dracula is the historical figure Vlad III "the Impaler" Dracula and transforms into
his monstrous alter ego to protect his family and kingdom from Ottoman Sultan Mehmed II.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
Luke Evans portrays the title character, with Sarah Gadon, Dominic Cooper,
Art Parkinson and Charles Dance cast in supporting roles.

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Principal photography began in Northern Ireland on August 5, 2013.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
Universal Pictures released the film in regular and
IMAX cinemas on October 10, 2014.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
Dracula Untold grossed $217 million worldwide and
received mixed reviews from critics.

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
The film explores themes of hero, monster, vampire, bite, bravery.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The tone is dark and intense.
